#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/chapter.rst:2
msgid "Explore the management interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/chapter.rst:4
msgid ""
"In this hands-on chapter, we will explore that the interface has been "
"significantly improved in GeoSever 2.15.2.x admin interface series."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/chapter.rst:7
msgid ""
"An enhanced interface to the integrated GeoWebCache is available in 2.15."
" You can now perform almost any cache configuration from the GeoServer "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/chapter.rst:11
msgid ""
"In addition, the security interface has been updated to track significant"
" improvements in the GeoServer security module. The good news is that we "
"will use the mouse more here than in any other chapter, so the keyboard "
"will not be used for the time being. Let’s get started. Log in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:4
msgid "Understand the interface of GeoServer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:6
msgid "After logging in to GeoServer, now focus on the layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:8
msgid ""
"As you can see in the screenshot below, the GeoServer Web interface has "
"three main areas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:14
msgid "GeoServer home page interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:16
msgid ""
"The central area is where the information is displayed; the elements in "
"it vary depending on what you do. After logging in, it will show you "
"brief information about the configuration data, as well as warnings or "
"errors that should be corrected. The version number is displayed at the "
"end, and there is a link to the administrator’s mailbox."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:22
msgid ""
"On the right, a list shows the capabilities of GeoServer. The acronyms "
"listed refer to the standard OGC protocol; We will discuss some of these "
"protocols in detail, each of which supports at least one version. These "
"numbers are links to XML documents that describe exactly what data and "
"operations are supported by each protocol. They are an invaluable "
"resource for customers willing to use your services."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:29
msgid ""
"On the left, a directory lists the configuration areas. Each area "
"contains links to administrative actions. When you click one of the "
"options, contextual options are displayed in the central area. We will "
"explore each area in the next paragraph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:35
msgid "About and status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:37
msgid ""
"This area provides information about run-time variables and how to "
"describe GeoServer to clients connected to GeoServer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:43
msgid "image42"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:46
msgid "Server status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:48
msgid ""
"The server status gives you a good understanding of the main "
"configuration parameters and information about the current state of "
"GeoServer. This information is organized in a tabular view. In addition "
"to providing information, this view allows you to perform some "
"maintenance operations. We will describe the main items listed in the "
"following screenshot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:58
msgid "Server status of GeoServer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:60
msgid "1.Lock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:62
msgid ""
"Using the transactional Web feature Service (WFS-T), the client can edit "
"the configured feature type. To avoid data corruption, GeoServer locks "
"the data that needs to be traded until the transaction is completed. If "
"the number displayed is greater than 1, your data is doing some "
"transactions. Free Locks button allows you to reset a suspended editing "
"session and delete all orphaned processes to release locks that may have "
"been abandoned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:70
msgid "2.Connect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:72
msgid ""
"This displays the number of vector data storage connections. Vector data "
"repositories are repositories configured for feature persistence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:75
msgid "3.Memory usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:77
msgid ""
"This shows how much memory GeoServer is using. You can run the garbage "
"collector manually by clicking the available memory button. This destroys"
" Java objects marked for deletion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:81
msgid "4.JVM version and font"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:83
msgid ""
"This is the version of the Java virtual machine (JVM) used by GeoServer. "
"You configured it in Chapter 2, getting started with GeoServer, during "
"installation. You will also see a list of fonts seen by JVM and "
"GeoServer. Fonts are useful for rendering space feature labels. We will "
"discuss this in Chapter 6, layer styling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:89
msgid "5.JAI usage and configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:91
msgid ""
"The Java Advanced Imaging (JAI) library is used for image rendering and "
"for better performance when GeoServer processes raster data, as does Web "
"CoverageService (WCS) and Web Map Service (WMS) requests. We will install"
" native JAI support in Chapter 11, “Tuning GeoServer in Production”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:97
msgid "6.Update sequence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:99
msgid ""
"This will show how many times the server configuration has been updated. "
"At the time of this writing, the amount of information is not that large."
" Developers seem to plan to use it to let you know that your "
"configuration file has been updated from outside the application. It "
"could be a rest call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:105
msgid "7.Resource caching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:107
msgid ""
"GeoServer also caches connections to storage, feature type definitions, "
"external drawings, font definitions, and CRS definitions. You can press "
"the clear button to force these geoservers to reopen storage and re-read "
"image and font information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:112
msgid "8.Configuration and directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:114
msgid ""
"This option is useful for updating the configuration without having to "
"restart the service. GeoServer keeps the configuration data in memory. If"
" an external process updates a file that contains configuration "
"parameters, you can force GeoServer to reload data from disk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:120
#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:129
msgid "GeoServer log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:122
msgid ""
"From here you can preview the current log file or download the full "
"content from the link at the bottom. It can be useful when you cannot "
"access the file system where the actual log files are stored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:131
msgid ""
"The record of each execution is also saved in the log, and the "
"configuration location of the saved location is in the global."
msgstr ""

#: ../../webgis-src/chc2_geoserver-management/sec01_getoknow/section.rst:137
msgid "log"
msgstr ""

